extends RefCounted
## Hand-made town maps. Edit freely: each string is one row of tiles.
## Legend:
##   .  grass/ground  ,  dirt path     :  paved stone   g  tall grass (wild beasts!)
##   T  tree          t  bush/hedge    ~  water         =  bridge / pier
##   #  rock/cliff    W  stone wall    f  flowers       F  fence
##   z  supplied wood fence          q  supplied stone fence (both solid, with gaps for yard gates)
##   _  sand          L  lamp post     %  lava          S  mascot statue (2x2)
##   a  shallow sandy water (walkable, at most five centimetres deep)
##   +  signpost (text from "signs", top-to-bottom)    $  hidden item    *  crystal shard
##   @  villager      v ^ < >  trainer facing that way   P  player start
##   1-9 named spots used by the story (see "anchors")
## Field obstacles (cleared with a beast's elemental power, see world_db.gd OBSTACLES):
##   w driftwood  j vines  d sand drift  o boulder  y dust storm  l lava  i ice  | ravine  x barricade  m fog
##   &  story gate (opens when "gate.flag" is set)
## Buildings are solid rectangles of one letter; the door is the middle of the bottom row:
##   C Beast Center  A apothecary  G beast outfitter  O trainer outfitter  K bookstore  R arena
##   Y dojo  M museum  U music hall  N fortune teller  E cafe  H house  Z your home  Q temple
##   X electronics  V Sky Tower  I Gearhart Tower  B cathedral  J bandit hideout  D music shop  h scenery building
##   s Cocoon Cove's Old Gear Shack, at the end of the dock (room "shack")
## Walkable tiles touching the map edge become exits to the neighbouring map (see world_db.gd).
## "heights" (optional): one more row of characters per row of the map, giving each tile its level (elevation.gd):
##   0-9 the ground's level there   ^ v < > a ramp rising that way, between the levels at its two ends
##   / \ a diagonal cliff across the tile (written "\\"): each half is on the level of the tiles along its
##   two sides; nobody can stand on it (tools/cliff_corners.gd cuts square corners into these)
## Neighbouring tiles on different levels meet at a cliff nobody can climb; ramps are walked along their slope only.
## Keep the back and the sides of a map high and its south low: the camera looks north. Every building, its doorstep,
## and everyone standing about is on level ground (tools/check_maps.gd checks). "cliffs": "walls" draws a town's
## cliffs as dressed-stone retaining walls instead of rock.

